# {{.Name}}

This project uses Modary's Admin Profile. The composition is explicit in
`internal/app/application.go`: general PostgreSQL, local development identity,
RBAC, session HTTP, and the consumer-owned `records` slice. River tasks,
governed Actions, audit, and MCP are not selected.

Set development configuration:

```sh
export DATABASE_URL='postgres://user:password@127.0.0.1:5432/app?sslmode=disable'
export MODARY_ADMIN_USERNAME='admin'
export MODARY_ADMIN_PASSWORD='replace-with-at-least-12-characters'
export MODARY_ALLOW_INSECURE_COOKIE='true' # local HTTP only
```

Run the backend:

```sh
go run -mod=mod ./cmd/{{.ID}}
```

It listens on `127.0.0.1:8080` by default. `MODARY_HTTP_ADDR` and
`MODARY_DATABASE_SCHEMA` select another address or application schema.

The Go binary embeds the production Admin UI, so running it does not require
Node.js. The source in `web/` uses React 19, TypeScript, Vite, React Router, and
an explicit Module registry. `src/App.tsx` composes session and route providers;
`src/modules/index.ts` selects product routes and navigation.

To customize the UI source, use the pinned pnpm toolchain:

```sh
cd web
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
pnpm test
pnpm build
pnpm assets:check
pnpm audit:prod
```

The build updates `internal/web/dist`; `assets:check` requires a byte-identical
clean rebuild. Bootstrap HTML uses `Cache-Control: no-cache`, while
content-hashed assets use ETags and `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000,
immutable`. A deployment therefore selects a new asset URL whenever its bytes
change without giving up long-lived caching for unchanged assets.
`audit:prod` rejects known high- or critical-severity production dependency
advisories through the public npm advisory service.

Run tests:

```sh
go mod tidy
go test ./...
```
